    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249-a2">

                <pb facs="0532" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 632.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 12,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 6th instant, respecting the freedom of the cattle in the
                    United States from foot-and-mouth disease. I have not failed to communicate your
                    note to the proper department of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
